(4245358, 609951, 22537, '<td valign="top">Another attempt at light painting. Only problem is that this attempt was rushed as I decided to slap something together in the last hour before the challenge submission deadline. Okay .... for the benefit of those who were curious and for the the kind comments given, this is how I did it.....though poorly. I inserted a glow in the dark bracelet into my cordless drill and spun the darn thing at low speeds in various parts of the frame, or what I thought was the frame in a pitch black basement. The wine glass was taped at the base but seemed to have vibrated with the bracelet slapping around the inside, hence the blur. Crap. The wine glass was not centered because I could not figure where the center of the frame would be because it was ..... hmmmm ....  really dark! Other than that, far too much fun and only a prelude to other shots which I hope will mystify future viewers. I''d really suggest others give this technique a try as it an artistically accesible side of photography that can yield amazing results.<br/> <br/>Finally, the title. W seemed like a nice letter that day.<br/> <br/>I''m done typing now. ;-)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-11-14 00:35:24.</i></td>', 'Another attempt at light painting. Only problem is that this attempt was rushed as I decided to slap something together in the last hour before the challenge submission deadline. Okay .... for the benefit of those who were curious and for the the kind comments given, this is how I did it.....though poorly. I inserted a glow in the dark bracelet into my cordless drill and spun the darn thing at low speeds in various parts of the frame, or what I thought was the frame in a pitch black basement. The wine glass was taped at the base but seemed to have vibrated with the bracelet slapping around the inside, hence the blur. Crap. The wine glass was not centered because I could not figure where the center of the frame would be because it was ..... hmmmm ....  really dark! Other than that, far too much fun and only a prelude to other shots which I hope will mystify future viewers. I''d really suggest others give this technique a try as it an artistically accesible side of photography that can yield amazing results. Finally, the title. W seemed like a nice letter that day. I''m done typing now. ;-)', '2007-11-14 00:23:20.000000', '2007-11-14 00:35:24.000000', 0),
